      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Some common things to consider when tracking asset depreciation beyond Straight-Line Depreciation are Accelerated Depreciation methods like Double Declining Balance (DDB) or Modified Accelerated Cost Recovery System (MACRS). These methods assume the asset's value decreases more rapidly in the early years, but they may result in a more complex accounting process. Additionally, you may also consider ensuring your depreciation calculation is consistent with industry standards, tax laws, and accounting software for accurate reporting, although straight-line usually suffices.",
